\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Proposed superpixel-GNN pipeline. \textbf  {Top row}: each 4-modality MRI volume is normalised, split into paired-slice units, and converted to SLIC superpixel graphs with 15-dimensional node features and two edge types (Stages~1--3). A 5-layer GraphSAGE network classifies each node as tumour or background (Stage~4). \textbf  {Bottom left}: five fold-best models are ensembled via soft-voting; predicted tumour nodes are back-projected to voxel space to produce the binary mask. \textbf  {Detail panel}: the GraphSAGE backbone maps 15-dimensional input through four 256-channel message-passing layers to a 64-dimensional embedding. Layers~1--4 apply SAGEConv $\to $ BatchNorm $\to $ ReLU $\to $ Dropout(0.1); Layer~5 omits ReLU and Dropout. A 2-layer MLP classifier produces the per-node logit.}}{18}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:proposed_model}{{1}{18}{Proposed superpixel-GNN pipeline. \textbf {Top row}: each 4-modality MRI volume is normalised, split into paired-slice units, and converted to SLIC superpixel graphs with 15-dimensional node features and two edge types (Stages~1--3). A 5-layer GraphSAGE network classifies each node as tumour or background (Stage~4). \textbf {Bottom left}: five fold-best models are ensembled via soft-voting; predicted tumour nodes are back-projected to voxel space to produce the binary mask. \textbf {Detail panel}: the GraphSAGE backbone maps 15-dimensional input through four 256-channel message-passing layers to a 64-dimensional embedding. Layers~1--4 apply SAGEConv $\to $ BatchNorm $\to $ ReLU $\to $ Dropout(0.1); Layer~5 omits ReLU and Dropout. A 2-layer MLP classifier produces the per-node logit}{figure.1}{}}
